===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|pinne}}, from {{inh|en|ang|pinn||pin, peg, bolt}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*pinnaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*pinnō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*pint-||protruding point, peak, peg, pin, nail}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bend-||protruding object, pointed peg, nail, edge}}. Related to {{m|en|pen||enclosure}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|pin||peg, pin}}, {{cog|nds|pin}}, {{m|nds|pinne||pin, point, nail, peg}}, {{cog|de|Pinn}}, {{m|de|Pinne||pin, tack, peg}}, {{cog|bar|Pfonzer}}, {{m|bar|Pfunzer||sharpened point}}, {{cog|da|pind||pin, pointed stick}}, {{cog|no|pinn||stick}}, {{cog|sv|pinne||peg, rod, stick}}, {{cog|is|pinni||pin}}. More at [[pintle]].

No relation to classical {{cog|la|pinna||fin, flipper, wing-like appendage, wing, feather}}, which was extended to mean "ridge, peak, point" (compare [[pinnacle]]), and often confused with {{cog|la|penna||wing, feather}}. More at [[feather]] and [[pen#Etymology_3|pen]] (Etymology 3).

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[needle]] without an [[eye]] (usually) made of drawn-out steel wire with one end sharpened and the other [[flatten]]ed or rounded into a head, used for [[fasten]]ing.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=9|passage=With '''pins''' of adamant  / And chains they made all fast.|year=1873}}
# A small [[nail]] with a [[head]] and a sharp point.
# A [[cylinder]] often of wood or metal used to fasten or as a [[bearing]] between two parts.
#: {{ux|en|Pull the '''pin''' out of the grenade before throwing it at the enemy.}}
# {{senseid|en|victory condition in wrestling}} {{lb|en|wrestling|professional wrestling}} The [[victory]] [[condition]] of holding the opponent's shoulders on the wrestling mat for a prescribed period of time.
# A slender object specially designed for use in a specific game or sport, such as [[skittles]] or [[bowling]].
# {{senseid|en|leg}} {{lb|en|informal|in plural}} A leg.
#: {{ux|en|I'm not so good on my '''pins''' these days.}}
# {{lb|en|electricity}} Any of the individual connecting elements of a [[multipole]] electrical [[connector]].
#: {{ux|en|The UK standard connector for domestic mains electricity has three '''pins'''.}}
# A piece of [[jewellery]] that is attached to clothing with a pin.
# {{senseid|en|lapel pin}} {{lb|en|US}} A simple [[accessory]] that can be attached to [[clothing]] with a pin or [[fastener]], often round and bearing a [[design]], [[logo]] or message, and used for decoration, identification or to show political affiliation, etc.
#: {{syn|en|lapel pin|badge}}
# {{lb|en|chess}} Either a [[scenario]] in which [[move|moving]] a lesser [[piece]] to escape from [[attack]] would [[expose]] a more [[valuable]] piece to being taken instead, or one where moving a piece is [[impossible]] as it would place the [[king]] in [[check]].
# {{lb|en|golf}} The [[flagstick]]: the [[flag]]-bearing [[pole]] which marks the location of a [[hole]]
# {{lb|en|curling}} The spot at the exact centre of the [[house]] (the target area)
#: {{ux|en|The shot landed right on the '''pin'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archery}} The spot at the exact centre of the [[target]], originally a literal pin that [[fasten]]ed the target in place.
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=iv|page=35|passage=For kings are clouts that euery man ſhoots at,<br>Our Crowne the '''pin''' that thouſands ſeeke to cleaue.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet|II|iv|passage=the very '''pin''' of his heart cleft}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[mood]], a [[state]] of being.
#* {{RQ:Clavell Soddered Citizen|scene=v|lines=1030–1032|folio=14|page=45|passage=Hee sett ''Promethius'', on a merrye '''pynn''', / Whoe dranke soe devillishly, that there he gott / A terrible heartburninge, {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:More Antidote|passage=he had made the sign of the Cross on his head; for he was then on a merry '''pin''' and full of jearing}}
# One of a row of [[peg]]s in the side of an ancient drinking cup to mark how much each person should drink.
# {{lb|en|medicine|obsolete}} [[caligo|Caligo]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Winter's Tale|act=I|scene=ii|passage=Blind with the '''pin''' and web}}
# A thing of small value; a trifle.
#* {{RQ:Spectator|III|295|February 7 1712|passage=He {{...}} did not care a '''pin''' for her.}}
# A [[peg]] in [[musical instrument]]s for increasing or relaxing the tension of the strings.
# {{lb|en|engineering}} A short [[shaft]], sometimes forming a [[bolt]], a part of which serves as a [[journal]].
# The [[tenon]] of a [[dovetail]] joint.
# {{lb|en|UK|brewing}} A size of [[brewery]] [[cask]], equal to half a [[firkin]], or eighth of a [[barrel]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Hugh Verity|chapter=2|title=We landed by moonlight|location=Manchester|publisher=Crécy Publishing|year=1978|isbn=0947554750|page=22=|text=Our ground crew were lodged in the main station, but they came to the cottage for a party when operations for the night had been cancelled and we had a new ‘gong’ (decoration) to celebrate. On these occasions we always installed a '''pin''' of bitter.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[pinball machine]].
#: {{ux|en|I spent most of my time in the arcade playing '''pins'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1949|title=Billboard|volume=61|page=82
|passage=Attracted by game operation, many invested heavily in '''pins''' and rolldowns prior to last spring.}}
# {{lb|en|locksmithing}} A small cylindrical object which blocks the rotation of a pin-tumbler lock when the incorrect key is inserted.
# {{lb|en|bodybuilding|slang}} An [[injection]] of {{w|performance-enhancing substance|PEDs}}.

